l bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could halt crown\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation only temporarily because Slovakia's improving  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic fundamentals will continue attracting capital from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 abroad in the long term.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The next possible factor for the market might come from the\par release of May foreign trade data on Thursday.\par     Slovakia's improving trade balance has been cited as one of\par the main factors behind crown firming, and analysts forecast the\par encouragi0r\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/euro unchanged at 39.900/940  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crown/dollar at 32.309/350 from 32.145/195  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5-yr yield March 2008 at 4.253/054 pct vs 4.274/074  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10-yr yld July 2013 at 5.152/002 pct vs 4.989/883  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040713e07d000pb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
