\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on July 13.  \b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2004\par 08:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 13 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Tuesday:  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  HOLDS REPO TENDER  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold its regular two-week repo tender. The market waits to see whether the bank uses the tender to influence the crown's exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 FINMIN HOLDS NEWS CONFERENCE  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Ivan Miklos will hold a news conference on the planned changes to the tax system.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO WEAKEN CROWN AGAIN  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday for the second time in less than a week, renewing its fight against the appreciating crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday the bank had staged its first direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May 2003. Last week's action pulled the unit down by 0.7 percent to the euro, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed firming on Monday, sparking the second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  round.  \par \par \uc2 KIA CONCERNED ABOUT SITE PREPARATION FOR \b \highlight22\uc2 SLOVAK\b0 \highlight\uc2  PLANT  \par \par \uc2 South Korean car producer Kia Motors is seriously concerned about a possible delay in the preparation of the site for its planned one-billion-euro plant in Slovakia, Economy Minister Pavol Rusko said.  \par \par \uc2 The Slovak government has run into trouble purchasing land for the Kia plant, which will be the country's largest green-field foreign direct investment ever, as several landowners refused to accept the price offered by the state.  \par \par \uc2 RETAIL SALES ACCELERATE IN MAY  \par \par \uc2 Slovak retail sales rose by a real 7.8 percent year-on-year in May, accelerating from 7.4 percent growth in the previous month, the Statistics Office said.  \par \par \uc2 INDUSTRIAL WAGES DOWN YR/YR IN MAY  \par \par \uc2 Slovak real industrial wages fell 4.1 percent year-on-year in May, after a 1.5 percent decline in the previous month, the Statistics Office said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 FINMIN SELLS SKK 840 MLN IN T-BILLS  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia sold 840 million crowns ($26 million) worth of 364-day treasury bills on Monday at a yield of 3.590 percent, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 For Slovak economic indicators  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see .  \par \par \uc2 For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20\par Budapest BUX        Prague PX50         Other related news:\par  \par   Slovak equities              E.Europe equities\par   Slovak money                 Czech debt\par   Slovak Indicators            Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Eastern European             All emerging markets\par   Hot stocks                   Stock markets\par   Market debt news             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   TOP 