\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  to sell crowns again.    \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2004\par 17:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 12 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday for the second time in less than a week, renewing its fight against the appreciating crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2 On Thursday the bank had staged its first direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May 2003. Last week's action pulled the unit down by 0.7 percent to the euro, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed firming on Monday, sparking the second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  round.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Igor Barat confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but declined to comment on details.    \par \par \uc2 Traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have bought around 200 million euros on Monday, a similar amount to Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on the market.... It is paying from around 39.800 up to 39.900 (per euro)," one foreign bank dealer said.    \par \par \uc2 Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  round pushed the crown to 39.950 per euro, from slightly under 39.800 where the bank started to sell crowns on the market. The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed the session at 39.900-940 per euro, compared with 39.855/875 at the open.    \par \par \uc2 The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been battling what it calls excessive firming of the crown for more than a year. It has repeatedly said the unit's advance was too quick and that it could hurt exporters in the new European Union member state.    \par \par \uc2 Despite its attempts, the crown has firmed by over three percent to the euro since the beginning of this year.    \par \par \uc2 The bank has repeatedly said the surge has been driven by inflows of speculative capital, but many analysts say foreign investors are attracted mainly by Slovakia's good economic fundamentals. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said there will be some room for crown firming in the long term, but they said the bank would continue using its monetary arsenal to prevent sharp market moves.    \par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might slow crown appreciation and keep the unit at weaker levels for some time, but they expected new firming pressure in the coming weeks on the back of more foreign capital inflow.     \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040712e07c0023a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
