\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on July 12.   \b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2004\par 08:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, July 12 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Monday:    \par \par \uc2  STATS OFFICE TO RELEASE MAY RETAIL SALES DATA    \par \par \uc2  The Statistics Office will release retail sales and industrial wages data for May.    \par \par \uc2  ECON MINISTER TO HOLD NEWS CONFERENCE    \par \par \uc2  Economy Minister Pavol Rusko will hold a news conference on incentives contracts with car producers PSA Peugeot Citroen and Kia Motors.    \par \par \uc2  CBANK WANTS TO REGULATE CROWN FIRMING    \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday to halt crown firming fulfilled the desired goal, adding that it was ready to continue correcting excessive market movements.    \par \par \uc2  Karol Mrva, the member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-making board in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, told Reuters the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the crown had firmed too quickly since the start of the year.    \par \par \uc2  JUNE INFLATION SLOWS IN LINE WITH FORECASTS    \par \par \uc2  Slovak inflation slowed in June due to the fading impact of EU entry and the lower cost of oil and analysts said the data confirmed the benign nature of price growth in the country.    \par \par \uc2  Inflation was 0.2 percent month-on-month in June, putting the annual rate of price growth at 8.1 percent, the Slovak Statistics Office said.    \par \par \uc2  Core prices, which exclude the impact of administrative measures, such as increases in regulated prices and excise taxes, rose 0.3 percent on the month and 2.3 percent on the year. June inflation was in line with market expectations.    \par \par \uc2  STATS OFFICE PUTS BACK MAY TRADE DATA RELEASE    \par \par \uc2  The Slovak Statistics Office said it would release foreign trade data for May on July 15, instead of the originally scheduled date of July 12.    \par \par \uc2  The office said it had pushed back the release of trade statistics because it needed more time than expected to process the data according to European Union's harmonised trade monitoring mechanism.    \par \par \uc2  For Slovak economic indicators    \par \par \uc2  For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see .    \par \par \uc2  For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click    \par \par \uc2  , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.    \par \par \uc2  News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403    \par \par \uc2  E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com    \par \par \uc2  Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20\par Budapest BUX        Prague PX50         Other related news:\par  \par   Slovak equities              E.Europe equities\par   Slovak money                 Czech debt\par   Slovak Indicators            Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Eastern European             All emerging markets\par   Hot stocks                   Stock markets\par   Market debt news             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par   TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040712e07c000wp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
