\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Slovak cbank says to keep fighting quick SKK gains.   \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2004\par 14:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 9 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday its direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday to halt crown firming fulfilled the desired goal, adding that it was ready to continue correcting excessive market movements.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in several waves on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the first such action since May last year, and dealers estimated it might have bought around 150-200 million euros.   \par \par \uc2 Karol Mrva, the member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy-making board in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, told Reuters the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the crown had firmed too quickly since the start of the year.   \par \par \uc2 "It is premature to asses the result... In any case, we think that it fulfilled the purpose why we carried it out. And, of course, we stay prepared to continue," Mrva said.   \par \par \uc2 The monetary body has been fighting against crown appreciation for over a year, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance was not justified by fundamentals and that excessive gains could be dangerous for the small open economy that joined the EU in May.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said the rally is fuelled by hot-money inflows, but analysts said the main reason behind the rise were Slovakia's solid economic fundamentals, which would drive the unit to stronger levels again over the longer term.   \par \par \uc2 Mrva said there was "some room" for crown appreciation in the longer term, but he added the bank wanted to regulate the pace of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movement.   \par \par \uc2 "In medium-term horizon, we see that the crown has tendency to strengthen... this is an attempt to regulate the pace," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "There will be some room for firming of the crown, but the pace since the beginning of the year was too quick. If it had continued for the rest of the year, it would have significantly exceed that room."   \par \par \uc2 Mrva did not comment how quickly was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  willing to let the crown appreciate.   \par \par \uc2 The crown has held between 39.900-40.000 per euro, its main reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , well off its record highs of 39.675 that it hit before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank stepped into the market on Thursday.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040709e079001fb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
