\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Slovak crown steadies, rand off highs.  \b0\par\par\uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2004\par 11:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 9 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown steadied on Friday though the market was wary after Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken it, the South African rand shied away from multi-year highs hit earlier this week.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday after the crown touched new record highs around 39.70 per euro , but the euro's recovery was capped at 40.  \par \par \uc2 Market sources said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been large by \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  standards, estimated to have been around 200 million euros.  \par \par \uc2 "(Thursday's) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was certainly aggressive, though I wouldn't rule out further action today given that the crown only weakened by 0.6 percent from its intra-day highs," said Caio Natividade, emerging markets strategist at Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Another analyst said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be willing to buy up to 500 million euros to try and get the euro/crown rate back above 40 and create more of a two-way market.  \par \par \uc2 By 0905 GMT, the crown traded down 0.13 percent at 39.95 to the euro .  \par \par \uc2 The crown has been driven up over the past 12 months by strong foreign investment inflows helped by perceptions that the country is progressing faster down the path of economic reform than its peers in central Europe.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trying to slow the pace of crown appreciation to maintain the country's competitiveness for over a year through a combination of interest rate cuts and market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  June consumer price inflation data on Friday had minimal market impact. The core rate was broadly in line with market forecasts rising 0.3 percent on the month for an annual rate of 2.3 percent.  \par \par \uc2 RAND RALLY PAUSES  \par \par \uc2 The South African nudged down from near five-year peaks hit on Thursday after the market failed to break under the six-per-dollar level.  \par \par \uc2 "There's a good amount of corporate interest to buy dollars around six and it's also significant that euro/dollar has come off its highs," said one UK bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The rand tends to track movements in the euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its main trading partner, though it has also found strength from soaring gold prices this week. South Africa is the world's largest bullion producer.  \par \par \uc2 "People have done well profit-wise out of the rand this week and are taking the opportunity to lock in those gains."  \par \par \uc2 However, the dealer added that pullbacks were likely to be limited to the 6.15/20 level before the market makes another assault on the six level.  \par \par \uc2 The rand was down around 0.5 percent at 6.08 per dollar .  \par \par \uc2 The Russian rouble edged down, but the pace of its fall slowed after Thursday's sharp losses saw it hit six-month lows versus the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Downward pressure has come on the back of growing concerns over the health of the banking sector. Earlier this week Guta bank, one of the country's largest by assets, had to stop paying out to depositors after running out of cash.  \par \par \uc2 It is now in talks for a takeover by the state-owned Venshtorgbank.  \par \par \uc2 Russia's biggest private bank, Alfa-bank, said on Thursday it was introducing a 10 percent commission for depositors who withdraw cash early.  \par \par \uc2 Local dealers said the rouble was finding support from a $200 million offer at 29.16 per dollar, suspected to be from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helping to contain the market in the face of strong dollar demand from households.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has $88.3 billion in its reserves from which it can draw to support the rouble.  \par \par \uc2 Rouble for settlement in the next trading session traded at 29.1165 per dollar .   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040709e07900128\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
