\par\par \b \uc2 Slovakia - Factors To Watch on July 9.  \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2004\par 08:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA, July 9 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Slovak financial markets on Friday:  \par \par \uc2 STATISTICS OFFICE TO RELEASE JUNE CPI  \par \par \uc2 The Statistics Office will release consumer price inflation data for June. The market expects headline monthly inflation of 0.2 percent, for an annual price of growth of 8.1 percent. Core prices are expected to have grown by 0.2 percent on the month and 2.3 percent year-on-year.  \par \par \uc2 C.BANK DIRECTLY \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  TO STOP CROWN FIRMING  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up its fight against the firming of the crown on Thursday with several waves of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The monetary body has been fighting against crown appreciation for over a year, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance was too quick and that excessive gains could be dangerous for the small open economy that entered the European Union in May.  \par \par \uc2 INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT ACCELERATES IN MAY  \par \par \uc2 Slovakia's industrial output accelerated faster than expected in May as machinery production and other sectors offset a slowdown in key car manufacturing.  \par \par \uc2 May industrial output rose a real 8.0 percent year-on-year, up from 5.0 percent annual growth in April, the Slovak Statistics Office said. In May 2003, industrial output was up a real 3.2 percent on the year.  \par \par \uc2 CONSTRUCTION OUTPUT SLOWS IN MAY  \par \par \uc2 Slovak construction output rose by a real 0.1 percent year-on-year in May, compared with an annual increase of 2.0 percent in April, the Slovak Statistics Office said. Construction output was up 0.3 percent in May 2003.  \par \par \uc2 For Slovak economic indicators  \par \par \uc2 For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United States and other Group of Seven countries, see .  \par \par \uc2 For a diary of forthcoming Slovak events, double click  \par \par \uc2 , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.  \par \par \uc2 News editor of the day: Peter Laca on +421 2 5341 8402; fax: +421 2 5341 8403  \par \par \uc2 E-mail: bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com  \par \par \uc2 Reuters Messaging: peter.laca.reuters.com@reuters.net   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For real-time index quotes, double click in brackets: Warsaw WIG20\par Budapest BUX        Prague PX50         Other related news:\par  \par   Slovak equities              E.Europe equities\par   Slovak money                 Czech debt\par   Slovak Indicators            Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Eastern European             All emerging markets\par   Hot stocks                   Stock markets\par   Market debt news             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par   TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par   TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040709e079000ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
