\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown weakens after c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2004\par 17:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, July 8 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown weakened by\par 0.7 percent on Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly on the market to stop the unit's rise,\par dealers said.\par     The crown firmed through a psychological level of 39.700 per\par euro at around midday on buying by a foreign bank, hitting an\par all-time high of 39.675.\par  \par     The jump pushed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy euros on the market\par in its first direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since May last year.\par     The bank carried out several waves of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with\par dealers saying they saw it selling crowns in a range of\par 39.700-39.950 per euro.\par     "They are still in the market, they are trying to drive the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 crown over 40.000. It is not working so far, but it does not  \f28 \par \par \uc2 seem that they are going to stop now," one foreign bank trader  \par \par \uc2 said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action would keep the market  \par \par \uc2 more cautious in the coming days and they expected the crown to  \par \par \uc2 hover at around 39.900-40.000 per euro in the near future amid  \par \par \uc2 fears of new \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 However, analysts viewed the current weakening as providing  \par \par \uc2 a good entry level for long-term players who expect more crown  \par \par \uc2 gains due to Slovakia's strong economic growth, government  \par \par \uc2 reforms and expectations of foreign direct investments.  \par \par \uc2 "Our long-term recommendation to buy SKK is still valid...  \par \par \uc2 In case of a second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wave, we recommend to further  \par \par \uc2 increase open positions," Komercni Banka said in a market note.  \par \par \uc2 - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1430 GMT-  \par \par \uc2 Crown/euro at 39.920/950 from 39.700/730 on Wednesday  \par \par \uc2 Crown/dollar at 32.210/251 from 32.150/190  \par \par \uc2 5-yr yield March 2008 at 4.266/068 pct vs 4.243/095  \par \par \uc2 10-yr yld July 2013 at 5.100/5.000 pct vs 4.996/890  \par \par \uc2 -.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040708e078001xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
