\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown ticks up, eyes c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2004\par 09:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, June 15 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown opened\par slightly stronger in a nervous market on Tuesday with dealers\par waiting to see whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would act against the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise.\par     The crown hit an all-time high of 39.780 per euro on Monday\par on the strength of the economy's performance and a government\par victory in European Parliament election.\par  \par     But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  talked it lower again, suggesting it\par could cut interest rates to  discourage inflows of hot money.\par     "The market will test the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's patience with the\par gradual shifting of the crown to stronger levels...  (But) we\par continue to see risk of real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Komercni Banka said\par in a report.\par     Komercni Banka said it did not expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par step into the market as long as the crown traded at levels\par weaker than 39.800 per euro.\par     The main market-moving factor on Tuesday will be the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's two-week repo tender.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had used the repo auction, its main\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 monetary policy tool, in the past to discourage speculative  \par \par \uc2 capital inflows by leaving the money market in a liquidity  \par \par \uc2 surplus and effectively pushing the interbank rates down.  \par \par \uc2 - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0745 GMT -  \par \par \uc2 Crown/euro at 39.790/800 vs 39.830/860 on Monday  \par \par \uc2 Crown/dollar at 32.956/33.006 vs 32.984/33.026  \par \par \uc2 5-yr yield at 4.55/35 pct vs 4.54/34 pct  \par \par \uc2 10-yr yield at 5.15/4.95 pct vs 5.17/02  \par \par \uc2 -.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040615e06f000yv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
