\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Slovak crown steadies after cb acts, lira dips. \b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2003\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 6 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown steadied on Tuesday after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw it retreat from record highs against the euro on Monday while the Turkish lira eased ahead of new foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered a sharp reversal in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown down to one-month lows against the euro, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying its gains were not justified by economic fundamentals. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marian Jusko also said the bank was considering tougher measures to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rising on speculative inflows. However, analysts remain sceptical the bank will succeed in reversing the crown's uptrend. "Jusko said he was looking to do more to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the whole market is bullish so it's pretty much useless," said Juliette Declercq, emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at JPMorgan. \par \par \uc2  Local dealers said they expected overseas players to take any pullback as fresh opportunity to buy, though Declercq added a note of caution ahead of Slovakia's upcoming EU referendum. \par \par \uc2  "I still wouldn't recommend building up short euro/crown positions ahead of the EU referendum on May 16/17, but if that goes through the bank will have to buy a lot of euros and have a lot of rate cuts to control the crown," she added. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak's are widely expected to vote in favour of joining the EU in 2004, but the worry is that the turnout will be below the 50 percent required to make the result valid. \par \par \uc2  Declercq likened the Slovaks' dilemma with that experienced in the neighbouring Czech Republic two years ago. \par \par \uc2  "In that case, the Czech's only managed to reverse the trend when interest rates came down to euro zone levels." \par \par \uc2  Foreign investment inflows have been pouring into Slovakia this year as the country plays catch up with its neighbours on the path to economic convergence with the EU. \par \par \uc2  By 0930 GMT, the crown traded a shade down on the session at 41.16 per euro . \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the region, Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zsigmond Jarai said on Tuesday that overshoots in the budget deficit could lead to euro zone entry being delayed until 2009/2010, from the current plan to join in 2007/2008. \par \par \uc2  LIRA DIPS \par \par \uc2  The lira's recent rally stuttered on Tuesday with the market running out of steam at five-month high levels against the dollar set on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The lira pullback coincided with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resuming daily auctions to buy $20 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost its reserves, though local dealers played down the material impact of the auctions on the market. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the risk premium that hit the lira leading up to and during the war in neighbouring Iraq had now been almost fully unwound, making further gains harder to come by. \par \par \uc2  "Turkey is still a high inflation country and nominal gains are going to cause trouble...We've seen a rebound but ultimately the nominal level of the lira has to weaken again to keep competitiveness," said Adam Slater, emerging markets analyst at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  Turkish April consumer price data out on Saturday was better than expected, though the annual rate remains at 29.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Slater added that in the near-term the high level of Turkish interest rates was likely to support the lira. \par \par \uc2  The lira traded at 1,536,500 on the interbank market  after ending Monday's session at 1,527,000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030506dz5600jx0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
