\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown ends down after cbank  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2003\par 17:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, May 5 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\par   clawed back slightly after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  knocked it\par one percent lower off all-time highs on Monday, and dealers said\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  looked ready for more volatility this week.\par     The crown closed at 41.150/200 to the euro, its key\par reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , compared with 40.810/835 at Friday's close.\par It was at 36.520/570 to the dollar, from 36.300/350.\par     During a London bank holiday that sidelined most foreign\par investors, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  began \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the crown hit\par 40.770 to the euro in early trading, and the bank continued\par selling crowns in a wide range until 41.230, dealers said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member in charge of exchange policy,\par Karol Mrva, said the bank did not consider the crown's strength\par was justified by economic fundamentals and that the room for\par further crown gains had been "almost exhausted".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ((please click\par on             for full \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  story))\par     He also said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in case\par of more speculative firming pressure, and repeated warnings that\par the bank would use all tools available to keep hot money away.\par     However, dealers said London banks would probably resume\par buying the crown when they return from Monday's holiday, and\par push it to stronger levels. That would spark further action by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which may include interest rate cuts later in\par the week.\par     "There will be more pressure... We will see more\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will eventually have to cut\par rates," said Slovenska Sporitelna dealer Vladimir Gajdos.\par     The finance ministry also failed to place all 5.0 billion\par crowns worth of one-year, zero-coupon bonds it had earmarked in\par an auction earlier in the day. Instead, it sold 4.0 billion\par crowns worth of the paper at an average yield of 5.4453 percent.\par     Yields on benchmark bonds fell. The five-year government\par benchmark  slipped to 4.695/555 percent, from\par 4.889/607 percent late on Friday. The 10-year benchmark yield\par   eased to 4.826/761 percent, from 4.891/826.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030505dz5500txu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
