\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown seen testing cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  nerve. \b0\par\par\uc2 436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2003\par 09:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, April 17 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\par   opened little changed on Thursday morning, but dealers\par said they expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to soon test stronger levels\par that could spark the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the market.\par On Wednesday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  knocked the crown off\par all-time highs against the euro of around 40.820 bid against the\par euro with comments to Reuters that it did not see a reason for\par the unit's recent steep rise.\par  \par     It said it was ready to sell crowns directly in the market\par if sharp jumps continued.\par     Trading was quiet on Thursday and many players have taken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  the day off due to Easter holidays on Friday, dealers said, but \par \par \uc2  they added that there were still a lot of offers to buy crowns \par \par \uc2  at around 41.000 per euro, and that strengthening was expected. \par \par \uc2  "There will be pressure for the crown to strengthen. I think \par \par \uc2  we could go (stronger)... I don't know whether it will be today, \par \par \uc2  because a lot of people are off, but in the near future, we \par \par \uc2  could go (stronger)," said Tatra Banka dealer Bibiana Valachova. \par \par \uc2  Valachova said she thought investors' high interest in the \par \par \uc2  crown could very likely push the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  against the crown in the coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have also said the unit's strength could spark a \par \par \uc2  cut to key interest rates at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly monetary \par \par \uc2  policy meeting next week. \par \par \uc2  "Comments that the NBS has recently made indicate that the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want to see the EUR/SKK below 41.0. If the \par \par \uc2  SKK firms below 40.9 versus the EUR we expect the NBS to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," said Commerzbank in a report. \par \par \uc2  "Furthermore, speculative pressure on SKK firming may result \par \par \uc2  in an interest rate cut... as early as its April 25 meeting by \par \par \uc2  50 basis points." The bank's key two-week repo rate currently \par \par \uc2  stands at 6.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  Most traders and analysts are bullish on the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  over the medium to long term, saying incoming direct investment \par \par \uc2  and strong economic fundamentals, including heady economic \par \par \uc2  growth and a spike in exports, are giving it room to firm. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The market will be closed on Friday, April 18 and Monday,\par April 21 in observance of Easter.\par -------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0650 GMT ---------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Crown/euro  at 40.960/000 versus 40.970/020 on Wednesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Crown/dollar  at 37.450/500 vs 38.202 bid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 5-yr yield  at 4.824/684 pct, vs 4.888/608 pct on Wed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10-yr yield  unchanged at 4.925/859\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030417dz4h00e1n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picsc