\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Slovak cbank bought 200 mln euro from banks in Jan. \b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 17:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, March 3 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly by buying euros from commercial banks in January to fight off speculative demand for the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to use offers from commercial banks when it bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth 200 million euros through individual deals in January," the bank said in its monthly monetary report. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to buy hundreds of millions of euros in the last months of 2002 to fend off speculative capital inflows that had been boosting the crown to all-time highs of 41.100 against the euro. \par \par \uc2  The bank's current bias is to resist a firmer crown, fearing it could hurt exports. Besides \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it also slashed 175 basis points off its key interest rates last year to make the crown less attractive for speculators and prevent the unit form gaining unjustifiably. \par \par \uc2  After the crown initially retreated at the end of last year, an improving foreign trade balance in 2002 and a decision by French car maker PSA Peugeot Citroen (PEUP.PA) to build a 700-million-euro plant in Slovakia lent it a new firming impulse in early 2003, boosting it to 41.200 per euro in mid-January. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence the crown either openly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market or by secret individual deals with commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  The banks may approach the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  when they have a large order, and it then decides whether to make the conversion off the market to prevent the deal from affecting the crown. \par \par \uc2  The crown lost ground in February due to the massive retreat of foreign speculators from central European following heavy losses on the Hungarian market after they unsuccessfully tried to push the forint  out of its fluctuation band. \par \par \uc2  The unit has been trading between 41.750-42.000 per euro, its key reference unit, in the past few days, but traders see it firming in the longer term due to expected foreign investment inflows and because of an anticipated convergence with the EU. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said data showing a sharp narrowing of the foreign trade deficit for January, released last week, could lift some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's opposition to crown firming in the coming months. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030303dz3300vo7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
