\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown falls as speculators flee region. \b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2003\par 12:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Jan 22 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown fell by\par almost one and a half percent in midday trading on Wednesday as\par foreign speculators ran from central European markets after\par being hurt by heavy losses mainly in the Hungarian forint\par     The crown traded at a two-month low of 42.100/170 to the\par euro, its key reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as of 1100 GMT, down from\par 41.510/550 at Tuesday's close.\par     "It's a regional matter. There were many losses in the\par region recently, so the mood is to close positions here now,"\par one foreign bank trader in Bratislava said.\par  \par     The main impulse for the flee of the investors were their\par losses in the Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The forint has fallen sharply amid the recent fight by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fend off strong inflows of speculative \par \par \uc2  capital. The bank's measures have included massive rate cuts and \par \par \uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown fall could stop at around \par \par \uc2  the current levels as they considered them as good a good place \par \par \uc2  to enter into crown positions again. \par \par \uc2  The crown is widely expected to firm over the longer-term \par \par \uc2  this year on the back of the anticipated inflow of foreign \par \par \uc2  investment and due to convergence play tied to expectations of \par \par \uc2  Slovakia's adoption of the euro. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030122dz1m00lm5