\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown bullish, mkt eyes  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2003\par 10:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Jan 16 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par   jumped early on Thursday, the second day in a row after\par it was boosted by French carmaker PSA Peugeot's (PEUP.PA)\par decision to build a 700 million euro auto plant in the country.\par     The crown was at 41.170/220 to its key reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par the euro, at around 0840 GMT, up from 41.360/380 late on\par Wednesday.\par     The unit hit a new four-year high against the dollar,\par trading at 38.975/040, from the midpoint of 39.100. The market\par does not often refer to the dollar as an indicator of crown\par strength, as the vast majority of deals are done in euros.\par     Early on Wednesday, Peugeot announced it would build a 700\par million euro plant in Trnava, western Slovakia, which is to\par produce 300,000 cars a year.\par     The news on the project, the largest direct greenfield\par investment in Slovakia ever, revived the market, as both\par domestic and foreign players immediately bought crowns.\par  "The bullish run (of the crown) continues.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The unit jumped\par to around 41.250 to the euro right after the open," said Tatra\par Banka dealer Bibiana Valachova.\par     "Now, at around 41.200, both bid and offer sides are pretty\par active, and it is a question which side will win. But if the\par crown breaks through the 41.200 level, it will then be able to\par firm even more rapidly," Valachova said.\par  She added that at the levels below 41.200, the market would\par start watching the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , who \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par market selling crowns and slashed interest rates late last year\par to fend off undesired firming on the unit, which it believes can\par hurt exports.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said it was not against a short-term\par appreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  imposed by positive news, but that\par it would fight against a longer-term rise of the crown, which it\par sees as unwanted at the moment.\par     Market watchers have expected the crown to strengthen in the\par new year as investors jockey for convergence plays that could\par yield high returns once the region adopts the single European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in around 2008.\par     Now in line to join the EU in 2004, Slovakia is also\par expected to draw direct foreign investment from western\par producers eager to tap into the country's cheap, skilled labour\par and proximity to mature western markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030116dz1g00ior\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
