\par\par \b \uc2  SKK firms after Peugeot picks Slovakia for plant. \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2003\par 17:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Jan 15 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par   firmed on Wednesday, as a decision by French carmaker PSA\par Peugot (PEUP.PA) to build a 700 million euro auto plant in the\par country offered the market a long-awaited boost, dealers said.\par     The crown rose to 41.360/380 to its key reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par the euro, up more than half a percent from 41.600/650 late on\par Tuesday.\par     The unit hit a new four-year high against the dollar,\par trading at the midpoint of 39.110, from 39.280/340. The market\par does not often refer to the dollar as an indicator of crown\par strength, as the vast majority of deals are done in euros.\par     The early Wednesday news on the Peugeot deal, which will be\par the largest direct greenfield investment in Slovakia ever,\par revived the rather sluggish market, as both domestic and foreign\par players immediately jumped to buy crowns, dealers said.\par  "This was the impetus the market was waiting for.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The crown\par jumped up to levels of around 41.300 to the euro on the bid\par side, and only then some profit-taking pulled it a little bit\par lower," said Slovenska Sporitelna dealer Juraj Zabadal.\par     "But I think this upward trend is not over yet. I think the\par crown will go stronger in the next days, towards the levels of\par 41.100-200 to the euro."\par     Early in the day, Peugeot announced it would build a plant\par in Trnava, western Slovakia, which is to produce 300,000 cars a\par year.\par  \par     The project is expected to have a significant positive\par impact on the country's economy, when it comes on line in 2006.\par     Market watchers have expected the crown to strengthen in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par new year as investors jockey for convergence plays that could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yield high returns once the region adopts the single European\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in around 2008.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Now in line to join the EU in 2004, Slovakia is also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to draw direct foreign investment from western\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par producers eager to tap into the country's cheap skilled labour\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and proximity to mature western markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the crown's gains are also expected to be limited by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par crowns and slashed interest rates late last year to fend off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par undesired firming on the unit, which it believes can hurt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030115dz1f00wqa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
