\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak cbank gov pleased with crown level-agency. \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2002\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Nov 27 (Reuters) - Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Marian Jusko is satisfied with the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown, after the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and slashed interest rates to knock the unit down earlier this month, news agency TASR reported on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The crown had surged on bullishness towards central Europe as investors expecting fat returns once Slovakia and other ex-communist states join the eurozone in around 2007-2008 raced into the region in convergence deals. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also boosted by a September election win by centre-right parties who have pledged to lead Slovakia into the EU and NATO, slash spending, and make other reforms. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped the unit in its tracks with a number of policy steps, and Jusko said he was satisfied with the result. \par \par \uc2  "Since we managed to fulfil our short-term goal - to stop the strengthening of the crown - I'm satisfied," TASR quoted Jusko as saying. \par \par \uc2  Jusko said the bank's longer-term actions would continue to depend on developments on Slovakia's wide external imbalance: "The important thing will be if there is a gradual improvement in external developments, improvement in foreign trade." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to knock the crown lower, in mid-November, and then bought over 500 million euros with crowns in direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a shock 150-basis-point cut to its key two-week interest rate, bringing it to 6.5 percent, which has since chilled market enthusiasm. \par \par \uc2  The crown hit a six-week low to the euro on Wednesday, as crown selling from local and foreign banks set off a small wave of stop losses. Dealers generally expect the crown to ease slightly before the year-end, as investors repatriate profits abroad and banks close positions to square their books. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy making bank board is scheduled to meet on Friday, but analysts do not think the bank will further cut interest rates due to the now-subdued mood towards the crown. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021127dybr00o2w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
