\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown falls on profit-taking. \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2002\par 17:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par  fell against the euro on Tuesday along with other central\par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as profit-taking following a recent rally\par coupled with corporate demand for hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The crown closed at 41.720/770 to the euro, its key\par reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , compared with Monday's close of 41.630/690.\par It ended at 42.014/074 to the dollar, from 41.980/42.040.\par     "The crown eased as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around us weakened as well\par well. It looks we will test the 41.800 level, though I don't\par think we will break it immediately," one foreign bank trader\par said.\par     The crown, still up around four percent since the victory of\par pro-reform parties in September elections, has eased in the past\par few days as foreign investors have taken profits on positions\par opened during a recent rally for the unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The easing trend has been also supported by emerging\par hard-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchases by corporate clients, which, some\par traders said, could be the traditional year-end repatriation of\par profits by foreign firms operating in Slovakia.\par     But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buying over\par 500 million euros in the market earlier this month and slashed\par its key interest rate by 150 basis points to knock the crown\par weaker, appears to have stabilised the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rate for the\par time being.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021126dybq00x15\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
