\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak cbank  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves jump to $8.9 bln. \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2002\par 14:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Nov 22 (Reuters) - The Slovak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves jumped nearly $500 million to $8.866\par billion in the week to November 20, the bank said on Friday,\par after a week of heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the crown.\par     The November 20 rise came around a week after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for three\par straight days, in which it bought around 500 million euros worth\par of Slovak crowns in order to dampen demand for the local unit.\par  \par     The bank's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves had risen by around\par $100 million to $8.44 billion in the week to November 13.\par     The bank shocked the market last Friday with a surprise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  150-basis-point cut to its key interest rate and analysts have \par \par \uc2  said it is possible that further rate cuts and direct \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are possible if investors continue to buy crowns. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained over seven percent since July \par \par \uc2  on the back of a reformist victory in September elections and \par \par \uc2  heightened enthusiasm in central Europe in general as the region \par \par \uc2  prepares to join the EU in 2004 and adopt the euro a few years \par \par \uc2  later. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   SLOVAK \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES    Nov 20     Nov 13     Nov 6\par    ($ million)\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               8,865.9    8,440.1    8,340.4\par  Commercial banks          1,278.4    1,590.7    1,578.1\par  Total banking sector     10,144.3    10,030.8    9,918.5.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021122dybm00p63\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
