\par\par \b \uc2  WRAPUP 1-Slovak cbank fights back to dent crown euphoria. \b0\par\par\uc2 810 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2002\par 19:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (wraps \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Fitch/Moodys ratings \par \par \uc2  from London/New York) \par \par \uc2  By Michael Winfrey \par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, sending the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than one percent lower in an attempt to dampen enthusiasm for the local unit which it believes is overvalued and could damage the country's economic health. \par \par \uc2  The bank's bid to tame the crown comes amid an increasingly buoyant mood in central European markets which have benefited from a constant inflow of foreign capital ahead of European Union enlargement. \par \par \uc2  Sweeping ratings upgrades by Moody's Investors Service for eight EU candidate countries and indications that a slight delay in EU expansion could help the mostly poor candidates save cash has also made the region look attractive to investors chasing higher yielding assets. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold crowns in several waves to push the unit down from record highs where it had climbed in recent days along with other central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in anticipation of EU entry in 2004. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak crown had jumped by nearly eight percent since July - also boosted by a victory by a reformist cabinet in September elections - as it took in its share of the steady stream of foreign funds flowing into central Europe. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had repeatedly warned in recent weeks that the unit was overvalued because of Slovakia's wide foreign trade gap and finally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after the crown touched another record high the previous session. \par \par \uc2  "We started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the crown was at around 41.120 (to the euro)," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Treasury Director Frantisek Szulenyi told Reuters shortly after the session opened. \par \par \uc2  Szulenyi declined to detail volumes used in the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but market watchers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have sold well over 250 million euros worth of crowns in a variety of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the day. \par \par \uc2  The crown, which hit a record high of 41.070/100 versus the euro on Monday, closed at 41.580/590. \par \par \uc2  BANK FACES BATTLE \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be the start of a long-lasting battle against investors who have flocked to the crown and neighbouring \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hoping to cash in on economic reforms and the convergence of candidates' interest rates with those in the West as the region creeps closer to accession. \par \par \uc2  "The Slovak crown has experienced a similar development as other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Hungarian forint, Polish zloty and the Czech crown, which have all been boosted by positive market sentiment," Commerzbank analyst Radomir Jac said. \par \par \uc2  "It can be expected that the positive mood towards the region will continue and the market will try to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stronger." \par \par \uc2  As evidence of the rosy mood towards central Europe, Moody's Investors Service boosted its ratings across the board for Slovakia and seven other EU applicants on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, EU Enlargement Commissioner Gunter Verheugen indicated entry for the candidates could come a few months after the originally planned January 1, 2004 deadline, which could save cash-strapped aspirants from paying billions in euros in contributions to the Union's coffers. \par \par \uc2  Moody's rival Fitch Ratings sounded a cautionary tone after the upgrades, however, saying several candidates still had fiscal problems that could hinder their EU entry. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the upgrades had been largely priced in, as foreign capital had flooded bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with speculative convergence plays and cross deals, but said it may have highlighted the strong positive mood toward the region. \par \par \uc2  "While it's helpful, it was fully priced in the convergence spreads on the eurobond market, and I don't see it having a large impact beyond augmenting the feel-good factor in the region," said IDEAglobal analyst John Davitte. \par \par \uc2  SLOVAK CBANK SEEN FORCED TO ACT FURTHER \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's attempt to weaken the crown may not last, as foreign banks were still hungry to buy the unit, and more action could be needed to prevent it from reaching fresh record levels. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fail in what it is doing now," said Jan Toth, ING's chief economist in Bratislava. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this level help close some positions foreign investors have in the crown, but after some time investors will realise they want some Slovak exposure, so they will buy Slovak crowns...and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will appreciate." \par \par \uc2  Analysts also said the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to have to cut interest rates to stem inflows into the crown due to their high differential with the West, despite an expected surge in 2003 inflation. \par \par \uc2  "The acceleration of inflation will be... outside of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  influence... There will be a certain room to lower the rates, and the room will widen in line with the pace of the crown firming," said Jac. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021112dybc00zyq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
