\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  dents  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown, lira down on Iraq. \b0\par\par\uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2002\par 11:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown on Tuesday, helping to bring it down from record highs hit the previous session, though analysts said the move was unlikely to break the uptrend. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Turkish lira extended its retreat from recent four-month highs against the dollar with the Iraqi parliament's rejection of a U.N. resolution on weapons inspections increasing nerves over a possible U.S.-led military attack. \par \par \uc2  Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  treasury director Frantisek Szylenyi confirmed that the bank bought euros against the crown at 41.12 , triggering a fall of almost one percent. He gave no indication of the amount bought. \par \par \uc2  "There may have been a shake-out of some crown long positions, but most people will probably just see it as an opportunity to get cheaper entry levels," said Koon Chow, central Europe \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at CSFB. \par \par \uc2  Chow added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be the start of an ongoing process, but added that he was sceptical whether it would achieve anything other than to slow the pace of crown appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "The market could well be back at 41, if not lower in a week's time," Chow said. \par \par \uc2  September's election victory for reformist centre-right parties and progress towards EU enlargement after Ireland approved the Nice Treaty last month have powered the crown up to record highs in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  Slovakia's high-yields - the main interest rate is at eight percent - have also been attracting inflows. \par \par \uc2  At 1030 GMT, the crown traded down 0.8 percent at 41.45 per euro . \par \par \uc2  In Hungary, October consumer prices rose a touch more than expected to an annual rate of 4.9 percent, up from 4.6 percent in September, providing backing for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hawkish stance on rates at its council meeting on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that despite a stronger forint, inflation risks remained high and there was no scope to ease interest rates from the current 9.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The numbers made little impression on the forint, with the country's high-yields seen lending it solid support in the face of deteriorating economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The forint was little moved at 238.50 per euro . \par \par \uc2  LIRA, RAND RETREAT \par \par \uc2  The Turkish lira was on the backfoot on Tuesday as investors opted to lock in recent gains as nerves returned over Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The Iraqi parliament voted to reject a tough U.N. resolution on weapons inspections, but left the final decision down to President Saddam Hussein. \par \par \uc2  "The Iraq situation is part of the reason for the lira consolidation as it brings us potentially a little bit closer to conflict in the Middle East," said Dwyfor Evans, emerging markets analyst at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "But there's also been some reaction to (Monday's) rate cut. We got 200 basis points, but the market was hoping for 300 or 400 and there's been profit-taking on the back of that," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cuts overnight interest rates by 200 basis points to 44 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The lira traded at 1,640,000 versus the dollar on the interbank market from 1,617,000 at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  Other high-yielding units were also in consolidation mode after recent gains, with fresh Iraqi tension prompting some investors to scale back their riskier positions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said profit-taking took the rand lower early on, but it ran into support after ratings agency S&P upped its outlook on South Africa to positive, and affirmed the country's BBB-long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating. \par \par \uc2  The rand traded around 9.82 to the dollar , broadly steady from late Monday levels. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty posted a bigger retracement, dropping back around 0.65 percent from recent four-and-a-half month highs under 3.93 to the euro . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021112dybc00m2m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
