\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak c.bank knocks crown off record high. \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2002\par 17:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Oct 23 (Reuters) - Verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled the crown down on\par Wednesday from the record high versus the euro hit in the\par previous session, dealers said.\par     The crown closed at 41.580/620 to the euro, its key\par reference \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , from 41.300/380 at Tuesday's close. It hit\par all-time high of 41.270/330 per euro during Tuesday's session.\par The unit was  at 42.620/670 to the dollar, after 42.270/360.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Marian Jusko said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par recent advance was not consistent with the country's wide trade\par deficit and warned the bank was ready to act if the unit rose\par further.\par     Jusko's afternoon comment reinforced a similar statement by\par the bank's monetary policy director Peter Sevcovic early in the\par day, who said the crown's firming was a bubble.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The crown and other central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained\par sharply on Monday on the inflow of new foreign funds into the EU\par candidate states after the Irish voted "yes" in a referendum on\par the EU enlargement treaty.\par     The crown has also been benefiting from plans of the new\par Slovak government to introduce austerity measures designed to\par curb the fiscal deficit.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  statements were not much concrete, and\par certainly not surprising... But mainly some foreign players took\par it as a signal and started to buy (euros). The highest matched\par deal was at 41.680 to the euro," said Slovenska Sporitelna\par dealer Vladimir Gajdos.\par  \par     "Before the end of the session, however, we saw some selling\par again, which sent the crown to the closing levels," Gajdos said.\par     He added he expected the crown to trade within the 41.400\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and 41.700 to the euro range in the near future.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021023dyan00t63\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
