\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank verbally  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to stem crown rise. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Peter Laca \par \uc2 472 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2002\par 16:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally on Wednesday to stem the rise of the crown which has gained sharply this week following a victory by pro-reform parties in weekend elections. \par \par \uc2  The crown had jumped by more than three percent against its key reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro, since Monday, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marian Jusko said the rise was too sharp, and was unjustified because of Slovakia's wide foreign trade gap. \par \par \uc2  "I am personally a little bit nervous about the development. There are some reasons for strengthening but what we have seen in the past two or three days is too quick, and too sharp," Jusko told journalists. \par \par \uc2  The crown started to firm on Monday on the back of news that four centre-right parties had gained a combined majority in weekend elections and had started talks on a coalition government. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the new cabinet could be the most pro-reform administration among central European EU candidate countries and that it could move quickly to cut the fiscal deficit, which should keep investors bullish on the Slovak crown. \par \par \uc2  Jusko acknowledged that the foreign trade balance had shown signs of improvement in June and July, but said the still-wide trade shortfall did not justify such a sharp firming in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as had occurred over the past few days. \par \par \uc2  "I am quite optimistic about the trade balance outlook but what is going on on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market now is not justified," he said. \par \par \uc2  The trade gap - the main reason behind the bank's cautious monetary policy this year - narrowed slightly on an annual basis from January to July to 48.9 billion crowns, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still considers it too high. \par \par \uc2  MORE FIRMING SEEN \par \par \uc2  The crown moved slightly weaker on Jusko's comments trading at 41.954/42.004 per euro as of 1455 GMT, compared with a five-month high of 41.860/900 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  But traders expect the positive mood to continue in the coming days, and said the market could now try to test whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to halt the crown's rise. \par \par \uc2  "I think the trend is for strengthening, and this will probably prevail, maybe with some corrections, in the coming days," said Slovenska Sporitelna trader Juraj Zabadal. \par \par \uc2  Jusko declined to disclose a range within which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to see the crown moving, and he would not comment on possible direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We will analyse the situation, and we cannot base this just on developments over a few days," he said. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could enter the market at around the crown's all-time high of 41.500 to the euro. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020925dy9p00muk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
