\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown firms, further strength seen limited. \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2002\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, July 23 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  firmed on Tuesday, but dealers said further strengthening\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  would be limited by political uncertainty ahead of September \par \par \uc2  elections and movements in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2      The crown was trading at 44.680/740 to its key reference \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the euro, at 0810 GMT, from 44.800/860 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  It was at 45.090/150 to the dollar, from 44.510/580. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the market could track the Czech crown \par \par \uc2   , which has eased recently after hitting all \par \par \uc2  time highs against the euro earlier this month. \par \par \uc2      "So far nothing significant has happened... If the Czech \par \par \uc2  crown stays in a negative mood... it should stop any significant \par \par \uc2  strengthening in the (Slovak) crown," said Tatra Banka dealer \par \par \uc2  Boris Somorovsky. \par \par \uc2      "Everything is in the hands of local customers. because of a \par \par \uc2  lack of impulses, it should stay in a range of 44.700-44.900 \par \par \uc2  (per euro)." \par \par \uc2      The Czech crown weakened slightly against the euro early on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday on continued speculation over possible covert \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through selected banks. \par \par \uc2  Investors often trade the Czech and \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair together. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said political uncertainty ahead of September \par \par \uc2  elections crucial to Slovakia's EU and NATO entry hopes would \par \par \uc2  remain the key driver behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the longer term. \par \par \uc2      Investors have retreated from crown positions just two \par \par \uc2  months ahead of the vote due to worries that the \par \par \uc2  opinion-poll-leading HZDS party of autocratic ex-Prime Minister \par \par \uc2  Vladimir Mecir could return to power. \par \par \uc2      Meciar was criticised by the West during his 1994-1998 \par \par \uc2  administration as undemocratic, corrupt, and chauvinist, and \par \par \uc2  diplomats have said his return would torpedo Slovakia's \par \par \uc2  accession aims. \par \par \uc2      "We should focus more on polls being released about possible \par \par \uc2  partners for a coalition after the elections in September," said \par \par \uc2  Somorovsky. \par \par \uc2      Meciar is expected to win the most votes in the September \par \par \uc2  20-21 polls, but opinion surveys indicate that other parties who \par \par \uc2  have said they will not cooperate with him can block him from \par \par \uc2  forming a government if they join forces. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020723dy7n00hwm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
