\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown opens weaker, seen calm, rangebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2002\par 10:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, July 19 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  was a touch weaker against the euro early on Friday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  mainly on domestic client activity, and dealers said they \par \par \uc2  expected it to trade calmly but to remain under pressure. \par \par \uc2      The crown was at 44.700/740 to the euro at 0740 GMT, \par \par \uc2  compared with 44.680/730 late on Thursday. It was stronger \par \par \uc2  against the dollar, at the midpoint of 44.040, from 44.385/440. \par \par \uc2      The crown hit a three-year low of 44.940 per euro early on \par \par \uc2  Thursday on heavy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying by domestic banks, but it \par \par \uc2  later rebounded as foreign banks took profits from their short \par \par \uc2  crown positions. \par \par \uc2      "We eased a bit early today as a result of a strong \par \par \uc2  overnight euro/dollar performance... Mainly domestic clients \par \par \uc2  were buying (cheap dollars) and some foreign subjects could be \par \par \uc2  seen too," said Slovenska Sporitelna dealer Juraj Zabadal. \par \par \uc2      Zabadal said the crown remained under pressure, but he did \par \par \uc2  not expect huge jumps throughout the day. \par \par \uc2      "The downward trend continues, but I don't think we'll see \par \par \uc2  big jumps. I think the crown will stay within the 44.600/800 \par \par \uc2  to-the-euro range today. But we might test the 45.000 level \par \par \uc2  quite soon, maybe within a few days," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit is now at levels where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support it in June. But dealers do not expect the \par \par \uc2  bank to step into the market again as current price movements do \par \par \uc2  not appear to be fuelled by speculative selling. \par \par \uc2      Zabadal also said he did not expect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action if \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued weakening at its current, slow pace. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said a range of 44.000-45.000 crowns to \par \par \uc2  the euro is justified by economic fundamentals, but it also \par \par \uc2  warned earlier this week that it was monitoring the unit's \par \par \uc2  movements and would be ready to act in case of sharp jumps. \par \par \uc2  The crown is expected to gradually weaken as Slovakia \par \par \uc2  approaches September elections that will decide whether the \par \par \uc2  country will be invited to join the EU and NATO. \par \par \uc2  The nationalist HZDS party of autocratic ex-premier Vladimir \par \par \uc2  Meciar - which is unacceptable to the EU and NATO - is \par \par \uc2  currently ahead in the polls. But analysts say it increasingly \par \par \uc2  unlikely that it will be able to find partners to form a \par \par \uc2  government. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020719dy7j00gz6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
