\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown flat in quiet trade, expected to ease. \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2002\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, June 21 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  was virtually flat at the open with no activity on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Friday, and dealers said it could ease in the near term but were \par \par \uc2  carefully watching the for potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2      The crown was quoted at 44.349/399 at 0755 GMT to its key \par \par \uc2  reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro, from 44.366/416 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  It was at 45.887/997 to the dollar, from 45.998/032. \par \par \uc2      The crown has eased in recent months due to worries over the \par \par \uc2  fiscal gap and upcoming elections expected to decide whether \par \par \uc2  Slovakia joins NATO and the EU in around 2004. \par \par \uc2      It dropped to three year low to the euro of 44.92 on Monday, \par \par \uc2  sparking \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank came into \par \par \uc2  the market again on Tuesday in a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that \par \par \uc2  ended with the bank buying crowns at around 44.400 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  "It's unchanged, no activity... We expect that we will stay \par \par \uc2  in a range of 44.300-44.600, and we could move towards a weaker \par \par \uc2  crown because of demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is quite strong," said \par \par \uc2  Tatra Banka dealer Boris Somorovsky. \par \par \uc2      "I don't think the crown should break the 44.300 level and \par \par \uc2  strengthen, I would rather expect it to stay in this range until \par \par \uc2  new impulses or new facts the market can use for further \par \par \uc2  trading." \par \par \uc2      The bank has said an exchange rate of between 44.000 and \par \par \uc2  45.000 to the euro reflects the performance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  economy, and dealers said they did not expect further \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if weakening came at a slow rate in that range. \par \par \uc2      "If the weakening is not dramatic, and if it is more or less \par \par \uc2  slow, I don't expect them to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But if it is very \par \par \uc2  illiquid... and there are aggressive moves, they should step in \par \par \uc2  to help the crown," said Somorovsky. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020621dy6l00g7t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
