\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown firms on another cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2002\par 17:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, June 18 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  firmed against the euro on Tuesday, after the central\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the session for the second consecutive \par \par \uc2  day to stop unwanted sharp losses to the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The crown closed at 44.35/40 to its key reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  the euro, from 44.48/52 late on Monday. It was at 46.73/78 to \par \par \uc2  the dollar, from 47.11/17. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on a sharp decline early in the session, \par \par \uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to buy crowns at around 44.700, \par \par \uc2  gradually pushing the unit up to 44.300 per euro. \par \par \uc2      "Nothing big happened after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We saw a small \par \par \uc2  correction to some 44.46/51 per euro, but then the crown settled \par \par \uc2  at the closing levels," said Slovenska Sporitelna dealer \par \par \uc2  Vladimir Gajdos. \par \par \uc2      "This time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was pretty agressive... I think \par \par \uc2  the crown will stay between 44.30 and 44.60 on Wednesday, if \par \par \uc2  nothing extraordinary happens," he added. \par \par \uc2      Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the third one \par \par \uc2  in a week. The bank started to support the crown on June 11 with \par \par \uc2  the first direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since January 2001, boosting the \par \par \uc2  crown from around 44.800. \par \par \uc2   The market expects the crown to remain under pressure, as \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has evoked speculative \par \par \uc2  trading with the long-term bearish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The Slovak unit is expected to see higher volatility with a \par \par \uc2  prevailing weakening tendency ahead of September general \par \par \uc2  elections, which are considered as crucial for deciding whether \par \par \uc2  Slovakia will join the European Union and NATO. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020618dy6i00u9o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
