\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown firms after cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2002\par 17:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      BRATISLAVA, June 17 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown closed \par \par \uc2  higher against the euro on Monday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted the unit from its three-year low \par \par \uc2  earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2      The crown closed at 44.480/520 to its key reference \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro, from 44.680/740 at Friday's close. It was at \par \par \uc2  47.110/170 to the dollar, after 47.080/130. \par \par \uc2      The crown, currently under pressure due to macroeconomic \par \par \uc2  risks and pre-election uncertainty, fell as low as to 44.920 to \par \par \uc2  the euro at around midday, and prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step \par \par \uc2  into the market for the second time in a week. \par \par \uc2      The bank said it had started to buy crowns at around 44.920, \par \par \uc2  but gave no volumes. Last Tuesday, it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around \par \par \uc2  44.800 and traders have estimated the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  volume at 50 million euros. \par \par \uc2      "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity to the \par \par \uc2  market, and the London players withdrew," one foreign bank \par \par \uc2  dealer said, adding he saw a short-term trading range for the \par \par \uc2  crown at between 44.400 and 44.600 per euro. \par \par \uc2      The Slovak unit is expected to see higher volatility with \par \par \uc2  prevailing weakening tendency ahead of September general \par \par \uc2  elections, which are considered as crucial for deciding whether \par \par \uc2  Slovakia will be invited to join the EU and NATO. \par \par \uc2      "Currently, the crown has no fundamental reason to rise and \par \par \uc2  (foreign) investors have no reason to run into long \par \par \uc2  crown-positions... I think the unit will remain under pressure," \par \par \uc2  said Tatra Banka dealer Boris Somorovsky. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it has an internal preferred range \par \par \uc2  for the crown, which can change according to economic \par \par \uc2  fundamentals, and added it steps into the market if it sees \par \par \uc2  unjustified sharp moves rather than to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \par \par \uc2  specific levels. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020617dy6h00wl2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
