\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown firms on better-than-expected Q1 GDP. \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2002\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      BRATISLAVA, June 13 (Reuters) - Better-then-expected \par \par \uc2  Slovakian economic growth data for the first quarter of 2002 \par \par \uc2  helped the Slovak crown to firm versus the euro \par \par \uc2  early on Thursday, but dealers said the outlook remained \par \par \uc2  uncertain. \par \par \uc2      The crown, which has been under pressure due to fiscal and \par \par \uc2  trade balance risks, was at 44.480/520 to its key reference \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro, at around 0840 GMT, from 44.510/570 late on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      It was at 47.150/200 against the dollar, from 47.130/200. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \par \par \uc2  crown on Tuesday after the unit hit 44.800 per euro, its weakest \par \par \uc2  level since summer 1999. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but dealers said \par \par \uc2  afterwards they saw persistent pressure -- mainly from domestic \par \par \uc2  corporate clients -- which threatened to push the unit back to \par \par \uc2  weaker levels soon. \par \par \uc2      Early on Thursday, the Slovak Statistics Office said the \par \par \uc2  country's GDP grew a real 3.9 percent, year-on-year, in the \par \par \uc2  January-March period, the same annual rise as in the last \par \par \uc2  quarter of 2001. \par \par \uc2      A Reuters survey of analysts earlier this week showed the \par \par \uc2  market predicting a real annual increase of 3.4 percent. \par \par \uc2      "The GDP data were good and perhaps it helped to boost the \par \par \uc2  crown a bit. We were about to go to around 44.600 (to the euro) \par \par \uc2  early in the morning, but then the trend turned around, to the \par \par \uc2  current levels," said Slovenska Sporitelna dealer Miroslav \par \par \uc2  Morhac. \par \par \uc2      Morhac said the unit was boosted by both domestic and \par \par \uc2  foreign players. \par \par \uc2      "Domestic clients appear to show some confidence to the \par \par \uc2  crown again, as they were already also selling (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," he said. \par \par \uc2      He added, however, it was hard to predict how strong the \par \par \uc2  current bullish mood was. The Slovak unit has been widely \par \par \uc2  expected to come under pressure again as the country moves \par \par \uc2  closer to general elections, scheduled for September. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020613dy6d00gze\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
