\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Turk Lira at new 2002 lows,Slovak crown calms. \b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2002\par 12:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 12 (Reuters) - The Turkish lira took another hit on Wednesday, dropping to new seven month lows against the dollar on growing fears that Turkey's governing coalition is in danger of collapse. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown steadied at higher levels after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inspired gains on Tuesday, with the main emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally trading with a subdued tone. \par \par \uc2  The lira fell around one-and-a-half percent against the greenback following comments from nationalist Deputy Prime Minister Devlet Bahceli on Tuesday, in which he renewed his warning that the government could collapse. \par \par \uc2  "The key question is whether all these political manoeuvrings undermine the IMF (International Monetary Fund) programme," said Gregory Kronsten, emerging markets analyst at WestLB. \par \par \uc2  "On the face of it they don't, but if market confidence evaporates and everyone heads for the door then it could cause problems," he added. \par \par \uc2  Bahceli's main gripe is over sensitive political reforms aimed at meeting European Union entrance criteria. He accused his two coalition partners of portraying his party (the MHP) as a force blocking the country's progress towards EU entry. \par \par \uc2  But the biggest threat to the coalition remains the health of Prime Minister Bulent Ecevit. Analysts fear that if he is forced to stand down it could be the trigger for early elections. \par \par \uc2  Ecevit appeared in public on Sunday, for the first time in over a week, but said he still needed a few more weeks to recover from the string of ailments that hospitalised him last month. \par \par \uc2  At 1000 GMT, the lira traded at 1,529,000 to the dollar on the interbank market from 1,510,000 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  SLOVAK CROWN CALMER \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown settled at higher levels after Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inspired gains, with local dealers saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action was likely to set a floor for the crown in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The crown traded at 44.54 to the euro up from Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of 44.80. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, tension between politicians and central banks in the region continued to simmer. \par \par \uc2  In Hungary, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said a government plan to set up a supervisory body at the bank was at odds with its independence and EU practice. \par \par \uc2  The new cabinet, which took power last month, submitted a proposal to parliament on Tuesday to amend the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law and set up a committee to supervise its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but not monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  "It's not so much the supervisory body as the government's interference on exchange rate policy that really concerns the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Natalia Gurushina, emerging markets analyst at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  "The worry is that (the committee) will be used as a conductor through which the government can influence policy," she added. \par \par \uc2  The bank has been at odds with the new government on inflation and exchange rate policy, with the latter keen to dampen forint strength that it believes is dragging on exports and growth. \par \par \uc2  A similar debate is going on in Poland, where the government has called for a shift in exchange rate policy in order to weaken the zloty. \par \par \uc2  So far Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stood firm in opposing a shift - policy cannot be changed without its approval. \par \par \uc2  Bank Governor Leszek Balcerowicz believes lax fiscal policy lies at the root of zloty strength, with a bloated budget deficit drawing in portfolio capital. \par \par \uc2  He repeated on Wednesday his call for the government to curb the budget deficit next year to help cap the Polish unit's strength. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020612dy6c00koj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
