\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown up as cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , seen stable. \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2002\par 17:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, June 11 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  reversed a six-week decline on Tuesday after the central\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dealers said \par \par \uc2  they expected the unit to stabilise near term. \par \par \uc2      The crown, which touched the 44.800 level earlier in the \par \par \uc2  session closed at 44.430/460 to its key reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \par \par \uc2  euro, unchanged from late on Monday. It ended firmer against the \par \par \uc2  dollar at 47.130/180 versus Monday's 47.230/270. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sold euros when the crown \par \par \uc2  traded at around 44.800, its weakest level since summer 1999, \par \par \uc2  and the action drove the unit up in the afternoon trading. \par \par \uc2      The bank's Treasury Director Frantisek Szulenyi told Reuters \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first since January 2001, was triggered by \par \par \uc2  the crown's sharp decline earlier on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      He would not disclose the amount of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  used in \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but traders estimated the total volume was \par \par \uc2  around 50 million euros. \par \par \uc2      "The strongest point was 44.250, but part of the move was \par \par \uc2  caused by stop-losses of those who were playing on further \par \par \uc2  weakening... Domestic importers then bought relatively cheaper \par \par \uc2  hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Robert Hakszer of CSOB bank. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should put a \par \par \uc2  near-term floor on the crown but most market watchers predict a \par \par \uc2  gradual depreciation in longer term, mainly due to the expected \par \par \uc2  uncertainty ahead of important general elections in September. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in the past said it has an internal \par \par \uc2  corridor within which it wants the crown to move, saying the \par \par \uc2  range could move according to economic development, mainly in \par \par \uc2  the external balance. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had now shown that the lower \par \par \uc2  end of its target range for the crown could be around \par \par \uc2  44.800-45.000, predicting no further market attempts to break \par \par \uc2  those levels in the near future. \par \par \uc2  They expect the crown to trade in a narrow range of \par \par \uc2  44.200-44.600 in the coming days. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020611dy6b00uka\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
