\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  boosts  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown, shekel soft. \b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2002\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 11 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the crown on Tuesday, acting on recent verbal warnings that its recent fall had been too rapid. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Israeli shekel dropped back close to last week's record lows against the dollar as Israeli forces extended their forays into Palestinian areas in the West Bank. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had entered the market to bolster the weak crown at the 44.80 level to the euro , triggering a jump of around 0.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Its not a huge surprise because they warned verbally last week, but whether it will prove that successful is another question," said Adam Slater, emerging markets analyst at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Treasury Director Frantisek Szulenyi told Reuters last Thursday that the bank would react if the crown continued to show daily falls of one percent or more. \par \par \uc2  "Its a thin market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traditionally been able to exercise some control. But the fundamentals still look pretty weak...I suspect this may not be the way to burst the speculative bubble that has developed," said Slater. \par \par \uc2  Other analysts said they were surprised the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came this week, with volatility not as great as it had been the previous week. \par \par \uc2  "I think it would be dangerous for the bank to be targeting a specific level with elections coming up, it would be better to stick to the line that it is volatility that worries them," said Jeff Gable, emerging markets analyst at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  Gable said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a high-risk game given the danger of speculative outflows in the run up to national elections in September. \par \par \uc2  Investors are worried about the prospect of authoritarian ex-Prime Minister Vladimir Meciar's HZDS party winning power - they currently lead in the polls. \par \par \uc2  At 0940 GMT the crown traded at 44.34 to the euro from 44.67 late on Monday and at 46.86 to the dollar from 47.16. \par \par \uc2  SHEKEL RESUMES SLIDE \par \par \uc2  Fresh Israeli raids in the West Bank kept up the tension in the region and helped put the shekel back on the defensive on Tuesday, after it bounced the previous day following a Bank of Israel rate hike. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked to be trying to halt the shekel's slide at around the five level against the dollar and did not rule out another near-term rate hike. \par \par \uc2  "The clear interpretation is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has drawn a line in the sand at five and is prepared to respond with further intra-meeting moves if required," said Alex Garrard, emerging markets analyst at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  "There was no data between the last two rate hikes, but its likely that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had some insight into how inflation was shaping up for May," he added. \par \par \uc2  The bank is worried about the inflationary implications of the shekel's fall over 11 percent so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Consumer prices jumped by 1.5 percentage points in April, for a cumulative rise of 3.9 percent since the start of the year - already above the government's target of two-to-three percent for the year. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded at 4.9720 to the dollar from 4.9550 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the forint showed little reaction to another positive inflation reading. Hungarian May consumer price inflation eased to an annual rate of 5.6 percent, from 6.1 percent in April, in line with expectations. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020611dy6b00k80\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
