\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to prop up crown. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Peter Laca \par \uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2002\par 16:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, June 11 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support its hard-pressed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first in more than a year on Tuesday, driving the crown up against the euro. \par \par \uc2  The market expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action to stabilise the crown in the medium term, but dealers were quick to say that the unit was still likely to come under pressure in the run-up to a crucial general election in September. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made good on its threat last week to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stepping into the market by selling euros when the crown fell to 44.800 to the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its lowest level since the summer of 1999. \par \par \uc2  The bank's Treasury Director Frantisek Szulenyi told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first since January 2001, was triggered by the crown's sharp decline earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  He refused to comment on market speculation that the bank would not let the crown drop below 45.000 versus the euro. \par \par \uc2  "I said sometime ago that we will act if the crown continues to weaken sharply... today's move was too quick, there were some deals done at 44.900," Szulenyi said. \par \par \uc2  He would not disclose the amount of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  used in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but traders estimated the total volume was around 50 million euros. \par \par \uc2  "The bank wanted to prevent the crown from testing 45.000, which seemed likely after morning stop-losses. I think we should see stabilisation now, between 44.300-44.600," said Tatra Banka trader Boris Somorovsky. \par \par \uc2  The crown has been on a downward path since the end of April when concerns about widening fiscal and trade gaps knocked it off all-time highs of 41.400 versus the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  By 1300 GMT the crown was trading at 44.470/525 against the euro compared with Tuesday's 44.280/330. \par \par \uc2  PRE-ELECTION PRESSURE \par \par \uc2  The bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should put a near-term floor on the crown but most market watchers expect a gradual depreciation in longer term. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in the past said it has an internal corridor within which it wants the crown to move, saying the range could move according to economic development, mainly in the external balance. \par \par \uc2  "The macroeconomic situation has not changed, so the market will wait for more data, like foreign trade, to judge the fundamentals," said a Bratislava-based trader at a foreign bank. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed its target now, so 44.800-45.500 per (euro) would be considered as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level for some time. But, we will check the 45.000-per-euro level again before the elections," he said. \par \par \uc2  September elections will be crucial for deciding on Slovakia's invitation to join the European Union and NATO, as a victory of autocratic ex-Premier Vladimir Meciar, currently leading the polls, is likely to impede integration chances. \par \par \uc2  United States and EU officials have repeatedly warned that Meciar's return to power would jeopardise Slovakia's chances for entry into the NATO and the EU because of undemocratic policies he pursued during his previous term as prime minister which ended in 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020611dy6b00jm3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
