\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown off record highs, seen stronger again. \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2002\par 17:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, April 12 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  closed flat on Friday after retreating from all-time\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  highs in morning trading, but dealers said a bullish mood on the \par \par \uc2  Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to push it up again. \par \par \uc2      The Slovak crown, which has been driven by the rallying \par \par \uc2  Czech unit in the past few weeks, closed at 41.43/47 to its key \par \par \uc2  reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro, unchanged from late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  It was at 47.10/14 to the dollar, from 46.94/99. \par \par \uc2      The crown briefly touched 41.33/37 to the euro on Friday, \par \par \uc2  but some investors took profits from the crown's recent uptrend, \par \par \uc2  pushing it weaker at the close of the day. \par \par \uc2      "I think the Czech (crown) will strengthen further, which \par \par \uc2  should also influence us again... We are still seeing bids (to \par \par \uc2  sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) both on the Czech and Slovak," said ING \par \par \uc2  bank trader Zuzana Rafajova. \par \par \uc2      The Slovak crown, which has gained over three percent this \par \par \uc2  year, has followed the neighbouring Czech crown as some \par \par \uc2  investors play the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  together and others hedge \par \par \uc2  their euro exposure through the Czech/\b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair. \par \par \uc2      The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in as many weeks to \par \par \uc2  knock its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down, but it has so far failed to weaken it \par \par \uc2  substantially from record highs of around 30.0 to the euro. \par \par \uc2   Dealers do not expect the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step into \par \par \uc2  the market to weaken the crown soon, with some saying the market \par \par \uc2  will watch 41.00 per euro as a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020412dy4c00vc8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
