\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown hits record highs, c.bank unmoved. \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2002\par 17:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, April 11 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  matched an all-time high against the euro on Thursday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  and dealers said its path following the strong Czech crown could \par \par \uc2  possibly lead to further gains in the near term. \par \par \uc2      They added that comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) \par \par \uc2  indicated that there would be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  crown to knock the unit weaker from the current levels. \par \par \uc2      The Slovak crown hit 41.45 against the euro at around midday \par \par \uc2  in medium-to-low trading volumes, matching an all-time high hit \par \par \uc2  exactly two years ago on April 11, 2000. \par \par \uc2      It closed quoted at 41.42/48 to its key reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  the euro, from 41.54/79 late on Wednesday. It was at 46.93/99 to \par \par \uc2  the dollar, from 47.24/28. \par \par \uc2      "We are still following the Czech crown. There was an \par \par \uc2  all-time high on the Czech crown (against the euro), and the \par \par \uc2  reaction on the Slovak was the same," said CSOB dealer Richard \par \par \uc2  Brza. \par \par \uc2      "I thought that 41.5 (Slovak crowns per euro) was a good \par \par \uc2  support, but it broke... I don't know where the bottom could be, \par \par \uc2  but 41.2 or 41.3 could be a good support. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the Slovak crown could range between 41.3-41.8 \par \par \uc2  to the euro in the near term. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Treasury Director Frantisek Szulenyi told \par \par \uc2  Reuters on Thursday the bank had no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against \par \par \uc2  the crown at current levels, despite a battle in the \par \par \uc2  neighbouring Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where that country's \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so far unsuccessfully tried to knock its unit \par \par \uc2  off of record highs. \par \par \uc2  Althought the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \par \par \uc2  Czech crown twice in the last two weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke \par \par \uc2  through the 30.0 per euro level for the first time in Thursday's \par \par \uc2  session. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not see the Slovak crown's \par \par \uc2  strength as having negative effects on the economy at present, \par \par \uc2  partially due to its relative weakness against the very strong \par \par \uc2  Czech unit, which is what is used to pay for a large part of \par \par \uc2  Slovak exports. \par \par \uc2  The two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  often move in tandem as dealers hedge \par \par \uc2  euro positions through the Czech/Slovak pair. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020411dy4b00tyc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
