\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown steady, seen testing stronger levels. \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2002\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, April 10 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  hovered near two-year highs against the euro on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Wednesday morning, with dealers saying the unit could test \par \par \uc2  slightly stronger levels if the Czech crown firms further. \par \par \uc2      The Slovak crown was at 41.52/57 to the euro as of 0730 GMT, \par \par \uc2  slightly stronger from 41.54/59 late on Tuesday. It stood at \par \par \uc2  47.06/12 to the dollar, after 47.37/44. \par \par \uc2      The Slovak crown has in the past few weeks mostly followed \par \par \uc2  the neighbouring Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which trades around all-time \par \par \uc2  highs of around 30.10 per euro, as investors tend to hedge their \par \par \uc2  euro exposure through the Czech/Slovak pair. \par \par \uc2      "I think we could test 41.50 (per euro) if the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not take any action and the Czech crown firms \par \par \uc2  further," said a bank trader in Bratislava. \par \par \uc2      "But I don't think any further firming (of the Slovak crown) \par \par \uc2  should be either very fast or significant, as we have already \par \par \uc2  seen what appeared to have been client orders to buy euros when \par \par \uc2  it (the Slovak crown) was at around 41.49/54." \par \par \uc2      The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its surging \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week and dealers said further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or \par \par \uc2  lack of it, will also set the direction for the Slovak crown in \par \par \uc2  the near future. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said they did not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to slow the crown's appreciation given \par \par \uc2  comments on Tuesday that the present strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  was not hurting the economy. \par \par \uc2      The  Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it will only \par \par \uc2  step into the market if it sees sharp volatility rather than \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against specific crown levels. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020410dy4a00g29\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
