\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown at two-year high, upside seen tight. \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2002\par 17:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, April 9 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  firmed to two-year highs on Tuesday on the back of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  record highs reached by the neighbouring Czech crown and \par \par \uc2  positive comments from the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the market sees limited room for further gains as it \par \par \uc2  expects local clients to begin picking up cheap euros at \par \par \uc2  slightly stronger levels. \par \par \uc2      The crown was trading at 41.54/59 late on Tuesday to its key \par \par \uc2  reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro, from 41.67/70 late on Monday. It \par \par \uc2  was at 47.37/44 to the dollar, from 47.65/79. \par \par \uc2      "The Slovak crown strengthened. The main impetus for this \par \par \uc2  was a strong firming in the Czech crown against the euro. It \par \par \uc2  reached its highest level against the euro ever," said Tatra \par \par \uc2  Banka dealer Boris Somorovsky. \par \par \uc2      "We are approaching an all-time high, which is around 41.5 \par \par \uc2  (Slovak crowns to the euro). There might be tries in the next \par \par \uc2  session, maybe tomorrow, to test this level, but if the crown \par \par \uc2  strengthens past that, it would be just for a short time, and I \par \par \uc2  would expect orders to buy cheap euros above these levels." \par \par \uc2      The Czech crown hit an all-time high of 30.05/08 to the euro \par \par \uc2  before retreating on Tuesday to close lower, erasing the impact \par \par \uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by that country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week. The \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown often tracks its more-heavily-traded neighbour. \par \par \uc2      The Slovak crown last touched 41.5 to the euro in early \par \par \uc2  2000, prompting repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) to knock it weaker. \par \par \uc2      But dealers said they were now not worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action after NBS Vice Governor Elena Kohutikova said \par \par \uc2  earlier in the day that the strong crown was not hurting the \par \par \uc2  economy. \par \par \uc2      Traders also said such a move at this level would be very \par \par \uc2  expensive for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which would have to expect much \par \par \uc2  more room to firm to justify buying crowns. \par \par \uc2      "To buy such expensive crowns would mean the expectations of \par \par \uc2  strengthening is much stronger than the 41.500 (to the euro) \par \par \uc2  level," Somorovsky said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020409dy4900w44\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
