\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown opens flat, seen following Czech. \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2002\par 10:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, April 8 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  opened flat on Monday, shrugging off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  better-than-expected inflation data, as investors kept an eye on \par \par \uc2  the neighbouring Czech crown for further direction, dealers \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2     They said the Slovak market was closely watching to see \par \par \uc2  whether the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CNB) would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  to knock that country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower, as it did last Thursday \par \par \uc2  after the Czech crown reached all-time high levels versus the \par \par \uc2  euro. \par \par \uc2      By 0740 GMT the Slovak crown was quoted at 41.70/75 versus \par \par \uc2  its key reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro, from 41.69/75 late on \par \par \uc2  Friday. It was at 47.52/59 against the dollar from 47.40/47. \par \par \uc2      "We started at 41.70-75 (Slovak crowns to the euro). There \par \par \uc2  has not been a move. I expect that we should stay at this level, \par \par \uc2  or maybe the Slovak crown could weaken, but it will depend on \par \par \uc2  the Czech crown," said Slovenska Sporitelna dealer Vladimir \par \par \uc2  Gajdos. \par \par \uc2      "Slovak inflation figures were very good, but we have seen \par \par \uc2  no move yet on the market. There has only been price checking." \par \par \uc2      The Czech crown has been the strongest influence on the \par \par \uc2  Slovak unit in the past few weeks. The two often move in tandem \par \par \uc2  because investors tend to hedge their euro exposure through the \par \par \uc2  Czech/Slovak pair. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, analysts said the CNB would probably have to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more forcefully to stop the Czech crown strengthening \par \par \uc2  to firmer-than-desired levels. \par \par \uc2  Data released earlier in the day also showed Slovak core \par \par \uc2  inflation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key monetary goal, was flat month \par \par \uc2  on month for an all-time-low annual rate of 2.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  Headline inflation was also flat on the month for an annual \par \par \uc2  rate of 3.6 percent. Both figures were well under market \par \par \uc2  expectations. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the Slovak crown to stick to a \par \par \uc2  tight range between 41.65-41.85 versus the euro, barring any \par \par \uc2  major move on the Czech market. \par \par \uc2  "A possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the CNB against the Czech \par \par \uc2  crown remains high after a not very successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  (last Thursday). If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown will weaken," Volksbank said in a report. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020408dy4800go2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
