\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown up, following Czech unit. \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2002\par 17:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, April 3 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  firmed in moderate trading on Wednesday, with dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  saying the unit was again pushed by gains to the Czech crown. \par \par \uc2      The crown closed at 41.63/66 to its key reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  the euro, from 41.74/79 late on Tuesday. It was at 47.28/33 to \par \par \uc2  the dollar, from 47.40/46. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the Slovak crown was watching the Czech crown, \par \par \uc2  which was testing an all time high against the euro at around \par \par \uc2  30.36/38 on Wednesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2      "Speculation on the Czech unit and also some corporate \par \par \uc2  client orders were behind the crown's strenghtening today," said \par \par \uc2  Istrobanka dealer Roman Trubac. \par \par \uc2      "It's still the same story... We're tracking the Czech unit \par \par \uc2  and it seems there is no other factor influencing the market at \par \par \uc2  these days," Trubac said. \par \par \uc2      The Slovak crown often tracks movements of the Czech \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as some investors hedge their euro exposure through the \par \par \uc2  Czech/Slovak pair, while overall trends in developing central \par \par \uc2  Europe also affect the Slovak unit. \par \par \uc2      Trubac said he expected the upward trend to at least slow \par \par \uc2  down in next days. \par \par \uc2      "We had said that already, and nothing happened at the time, \par \par \uc2  but now it really seems that the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to \par \par \uc2  be forced to act (to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), which \par \par \uc2  would of course also stop \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown's firming," he added. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020403dy4300upx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
