\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty lower on Polish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  concerns. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robin Shepherd \par \uc2 808 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 12:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 1 (Reuters) - The zloty edged down to two and half week lows against the euro on Friday amid renewed concerns over the independence of the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the neighbouring Czech Republic, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also in focus. Thursday's meeting of the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised markets by the absence of any hardline comment aimed at talking down the ever resilient crown. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected appreciation pressure on the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but were mindful of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's proven readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to prevent any sharp firming. \par \par \uc2  Hungarian growth figures had little effect on the forint with market attention directed towards forthcoming elections. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Russian rouble continued to hover just below 31 to the dollar and the South African rand firmed slightly on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments and the affirmation of the country's credit ratings by Standard & Poors. \par \par \uc2  POLISH \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  INDEPENDENCE \par \par \uc2  The zloty edged lower to 3.6720 to the euro as the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence dominated concerns. \par \par \uc2  The Polish parliament on Friday resumes discussions over a resolution scolding the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for damaging the economy with high interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The move follows Wednesday's controversial decision by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave rates on hold. The main Polish market rate stands at 10 percent, 6.5 percentage points above inflation. \par \par \uc2  "This is not going to help the zloty but I don't think it will crush it either unless they do something really drastic with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Investors are waiting to see if the resolution will be followed by a bill, proposed by junior goverment coalition members, aimed at watering down the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation fighting mandate and adding more dovish members to the 10-seat rate-setting panel. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said worse-than-expected current account deficit figures for January, which showed the monthly shortfall widening to $826 million from $500 million in December, also weighed on the Polish unit on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown opened steady versus the euro but analysts said they expected the 31.50 level to be tested within the next few days after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained a stony silence on the robustness of the crown. \par \par \uc2  The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  set a two-month high just shy of 31.5 on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates unchanged and kept the market guessing as to if and when it might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken what it says is an overvalued crown. \par \par \uc2  "That was a surprise. I get the feeling everyone was expecting them to talk down the crown," said Dwyfor Evans, emerging market economist at Bank of America. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government officials are concerned that a stronger crown - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already hit all time highs against the euro in recent months - would undermine the country's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Vice-Governor Ludek Niedermayer said after the bank's monetary policy meeting on Thursday the bank was not overly concerned about day to day market volatility and stuck to the standard policy line the bank can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if and when needed. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gone in directly or verbally in the last three or four months. The market knows that should euro/Czech fall below 31.50 there's likely to be some form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Evans. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown fell off highs early on Friday as the market reacted negatively to Thursday's news that there was only one bid for gas company SPP in Slovakia's biggest ever privatisation. \par \par \uc2  The crown was quoted at 41.75/80 to its key reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro. On Thursday, the Slovak government received a sole bid for 49 percent and management control over SPP from a consortium of Gaz de France , Russian Gazprom and Germany's Ruhrgas. \par \par \uc2  A source close to the deal said the offered price was below, but close to, analysts' valuation of the deal of $3.0 billion. \par \par \uc2  Having recoverd a little from month and a half lows against the euro on Wednesday the Hungarian forint was again looking a little weaker. It was trading around 245.90 to the euro . \par \par \uc2  Hungary's gross domestic product (GDP) growth slowed to 3.8 percent in 2001 according to preliminary data, from 5.2 percent in the previous year, according to figures out on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The rand firmed about three cents to the dollar at 11.37, heartened by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's confirmation that its net open forward position (NOFP), a measure of its uncovered \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  liabilities, had fallen to $2.99 billion from $4.8 billion in December. \par \par \uc2  The unit was also supported by rating agency Standard & Poor's affirmation of the country's BBB-minus/A-3 foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign credit rating. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020301dy3100lgc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
