\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Czech, Slovak crowns probe higher. \b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2002\par 11:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 22 (Reuters) - The Czech crown hit its highest levels in a week against the euro on Friday on reports of good foreign demand and receding nerves over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown rose alongside its Czech counterpart, buoyed by good news on the privatisation front earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  The crown has drifted steadily higher this week despite a stern warning against excessive strength from Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Oldrich Dedek in a Reuters interview last week. \par \par \uc2  Dedek said the crown should fall to around 33 to the euro and warned that the bank was prepared to fight \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength with all means available to it, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  However, one dealer in London said he didn't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in around current levels. \par \par \uc2  "I still think we are some way from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I don't see them coming in ahead of the 31.50 level," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Czech January trade data added to the mildly positive tone, with the deficit coming in a shade below expectations at 6.57 billion crowns. \par \par \uc2  Technical analysts are cautious on the near-term outlook for the euro/crown rate, saying the bias remains to the downside for the euro. \par \par \uc2  "It could be that we're hammering out a bottom, but I wouldn't say I'm bullish - we're still in a downward sloping trend channel," said Steve Wesiak, technical analyst at ABN Amro in Amsterdam. \par \par \uc2  Wesiak said key support lies around 31.46 crowns per euro, but that the market needed to take out resistance around 32.675 and then just below 33 to turn the outlook more positive. \par \par \uc2  At 1045 GMT, the crown traded at 31.735 to the euro from 31.79 and at 36.457 to the dollar from 36.465. \par \par \uc2  SLOVAK CROWN BUOYANT \par \par \uc2  The Slovak crown was also on the up, continuing to attract demand after good news earlier in the week on the government's plans to sell a 49 percent stake in gas monopoly SPP. \par \par \uc2  The leftist SDL, a member of the coalition government, had been pushing for the stake to be cut to 24 percent, but withdrew its objection to the sale without the reduction. \par \par \uc2  Final bids for the stake, which could rake in as much as $3 billion, are due by February 28, with France's TotalFinaElf seen as one of six likely bidders. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts don't see the crown's current strength giving the authorities as much cause for concern as in the Czech case. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the break of 42 (crowns per euro) is likely to prompt verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and there are lots of things that could take the heat out the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Stephen Gilmore, emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley. \par \par \uc2  Gilmore said a possible deterioration in Slovakia's current account position and nerves ahead of September elections were potential negatives for the crown, but he added that the bank remained positive on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the long term. \par \par \uc2  The crown traded at 41.90 to the euro from 42.11 and at 48.24 to the dollar from 48.38. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020222dy2m00ku7\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \